{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"scathing-custommade-bobcat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"SITE: src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py run_sweep(tracker) — 'repo_root = os.path.dirname(tracker)' (sanctioned '# repo-root-ok:' in the AC#4 guard check_repo_root_from_tracker.py as the ONE deferred site).\n\nCONTEXT: split off from auspicial-friended-merganser (2ec7-be89-9b01-496a), which fixed the 8 clean os.path.dirname(tracker)-as-config-root sites. run_sweep is the DETACHED-CHILD compaction entry point: it is spawned with cwd == the STORE (StorePaths(tracker).canonical) and inherits only 'tracker' as its handle. It cannot cleanly discover the CODE root:\n  - cwd is the store (itself a git repo), so git-toplevel discovery finds the WRONG root;\n  - REBAR_ROOT may not be set on the MCP deployment.\n\nWHY DEFERRED (design decision, not a mechanical fix): giving run_sweep a correct code root needs a spawn-contract change — e.g. the parent (maybe_compact, which HAS repo_root) passes the resolved code root to the detached child via argv/env, and run_sweep threads it into compose_config. That is a new interface decision (how the detached worker receives its code root), so it exceeds the behavior-preserving/localized bar of the parent ticket.\n\nIMPACT (milder than the parent's AC#1): on a relocated store run_sweep reads DEFAULT compaction config (compact_all_cli's compaction thresholds), not a silently-disabled enforcement gate. Compaction still runs; it just ignores a non-default [compact] config. No gate is disabled.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n1. run_sweep resolves the code/config root independent of where the store lives (via a spawn-contract change carrying the resolved root from maybe_compact to the detached child, or an equivalent design).\n2. On a relocated store with a non-default [compact] config, run_sweep honours it (RED->GREEN test).\n3. Remove the '# repo-root-ok:' sanction from compact_trigger.py once fixed; the AC#4 guard (scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py) then has ZERO allowlisted sites.\n4. Caused-by attribution: same origin class as the parent (dirname(tracker)-as-config-root construct).","id":"6bf1-326b-7404-4034","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"run_sweep detached child derives repo_root from os.path.dirname(tracker), ignoring relocated-store config"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787939368830168001,"uuid":"e44c3c08-bcdc-494d-9e45-1ec28140ba17"}